,title,link,text,language,family
0,Akan | World Mission Media,https://worldmission.media/languages-of-the-world/akan,"Akan, a language with rich oral traditions, belongs to the Kwa branch of the Niger-Congo language family. Predominantly spoken in Ghana and the Ivory Coast, it includes several dialects like Twi and Fante. Akan is spoken by about 22 million people.",Akan,Niger-Congo
1,(PDF) Construing Joy as Body Parts in Akan: Synergizing Conceptual...,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/380945395_Construing_Joy_as_Body_Parts_in_Akan_Synergizing_Conceptual_Metaphor_and_Transitivity_Analyses,Kwa branch of the Niger-Congo phylum. The Akan language cluster includes closely. related dialects spoken in the Southern parts of Ghana as well as some parts of Cote.,Akan,Niger-Congo
2,Akan Translation Services in South Africa | Premium Lingua,https://premiumlingua.co.za/language-akan/,"Akan is a member of the Niger-Congo language family, primarily spoken in West Africa. The language carries deep cultural significance for its speakers and plays an important role in preserving the identity and heritage of the communities that use it.",Akan,Niger-Congo
3,Acquisition of consonants among typically developing Akan-speaking...,https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33337249/,"This paper investigates the development of consonants in Akan among typically developing children aged 3-5 years. Method: A list of 103 Akan words was compiled, sampling the full range of prosodic structures, sound positions, features and segments, and controlling for word familiarity.",Akan,Niger-Congo
